course: dictionary
lesson: 2500
title: Debit and money words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A debit is money taken out of a bank account. In «A direct debit lets a company take a bill from the bank account automatically», the clues are «take» and «bank account», so the money leaves the account by itself.
explain: To check, ask what word would fit. Money going out fits the sentence. Money coming in does not.
explain: Debit is the opposite of credit. «A debit card spends money already in the account; a credit card borrows money that must be paid back later.» Debit spends money you already have, and credit borrows money you must pay back.
fact: A debit is money taken out of a bank account.
fact: To debit an account means to take money out of it.
fact: A direct debit is an automatic payment from a bank account, often for bills each month.
fact: A debit card takes money straight from your own bank account when you pay.
fact: In accounting, debit is the side of a record showing money paid out, and credit is the opposite.
exercise: «A debit card spends money already in the account; a credit card borrows money that must be paid back later.» Where does a debit card take its money from? | A card company loan | A shop's till | *Your own bank account | A friend
exercise: Ella reads, «A direct debit pays a bill each month automatically.» What does direct debit mean? | A holiday from school | A bill you pay in cash at a shop | *An automatic payment taken from a bank account | Money given to you by a bank
exercise: In maths, Sam sees debits marked as minus. What does a debit do in a money sum? | Adds money to the total | Doubles the money | *Takes money away, like subtract | Changes the colour of the bill
test: What does it mean to debit an account? | To close it forever | To check the balance only | To put money into it | *To take money out of it
test: Which word is the opposite of debit? | Direct | *Credit | Bill | Account
exam: Why does the money seem to vanish in «by direct debit, so the money seems to vanish without anyone paying at a till»? | Because the bank gives it back | *Because it is taken out automatically without anyone paying at a till | Because it turns into a credit card | Because the bill was paid in cash
